It can work both ways.  The system will not remember anything
good which happened since the save, either.  I had my Windows
system rebooted in the middle of the game I'm in now; recovery
worked fine, but I'd just entered Medusa's, where my pet
(arch-Lich) had taken out the Titan, and I'd arranged for the
giant that was there to provide me with an extra boulder or two
for crossing the water.  The restore took me back in time, to
the moment I'd just entered the level, and my pet promptly took
out the giant first, before he could provide me with the
boulder.  (IIRC, he did leave a boulder, but it was against the
right wall, so totally useless.  But it worked out all right in
the end, as there were a couple of giants on the islands, and I
didn't let my pet get at them before they'd sent a couple of
boulders my way.)

